<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salinguerra II Torelli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1160–1244</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salinguerra II Torelli was the leader of the Ghibelline Torelli family in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> and for decades the city's dominant figure. He fought the Guelph Este marquises for control of the commune and allied himself with Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>. In 1240 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azzo-vii-deste">Azzo VII d'Este</a>, with papal and Venetian help, captured Ferrara and took him prisoner; he died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, opening the way to Este lordship.</p></div>
